00:39:13.070 --> 00:39:15.070
So let's get into a little
bit more in the data.

00:39:17.580 --> 00:39:19.640
So what if you
actually have someone--

00:39:19.640 --> 00:39:22.400
let's say 18 years old,
a CEO for a company.

00:39:22.400 --> 00:39:25.670
That would be really easy
to identify that person.

00:39:25.670 --> 00:39:29.710
So what we did is I have
equity here I could run.

00:39:29.710 --> 00:39:33.460
And you could see the part
of DLP using packeting.

00:39:33.460 --> 00:39:37.480
We could actually pretty much
transform all those records

00:39:37.480 --> 00:39:39.010
to thousands of records.

00:39:51.370 --> 00:39:54.380
So you could see that--

00:39:54.380 --> 00:39:56.460
so first thing you notice,
the cardholder's name.

00:39:56.460 --> 00:39:58.920
It's actually
completely tokenized.

00:39:58.920 --> 00:40:00.960
So we are using a
crypto hash algorithm

00:40:00.960 --> 00:40:03.490
