00:42:41.210 --> 00:42:44.480
So as Masud just said,
this is all open source.

00:42:44.480 --> 00:42:48.410
The goal of those is to
give you the building blocks

00:42:48.410 --> 00:42:51.830
to be able to add DLP as part
of your ingestion process.

00:42:51.830 --> 00:42:55.910
So we showed a
UI-based demo today.

00:42:55.910 --> 00:42:56.870
You can start this.

00:42:56.870 --> 00:42:58.730
You can really use
this as building block,

00:42:58.730 --> 00:43:02.000
create your ingestion pipeline,
or add it to your ingestion

00:43:02.000 --> 00:43:05.760
pipeline that you already have.

00:43:05.760 --> 00:43:09.500
So as you go, adding more of
those ingestion pipelines,

00:43:09.500 --> 00:43:12.400
you can use this,
add de-identification

00:43:12.400 --> 00:43:15.680
that really enables you to bring
more data into the analytics

00:43:15.680 --> 00:43:19.730
product without having to
worry how you will add this,

00:43:19.730 --> 00:43:22.070
or without doing
de-identification

00:43:22.070 --> 00:43:23.430
after the fact.

00:43:23.430 --> 00:43:26.345
So if you want information
on the open source repo,

00:43:26.345 --> 00:43:28.220
where to find it, how
